{{!-- A damage roll's body: the roll itself, and — when the message carries target ids in its
      SYSTEM_ID "targets" flag — the Warden's Apply control, which `renderChatMessageHTML` wires
      and hides from everyone else.

      The roll is rendered here rather than left to core. Core rebuilds a roll message's block from
      `message.rolls` only while the stored content has no element children (ChatMessage
      #renderRollContent); a card body has children, so the card renders the roll itself. The label
      is the message's flavor, so it is the caption.

      A trap's damage (`[[/damage d6 STR]]`) carries an `attribute`: it comes off that attribute
      and not HP, and its second button applies it with armour not helping. --}}
{{{rollHTML}}}
{{#if hasTargets}}
{{#if attribute}}
<button type="button" class="cairn-card-action apply-dmg">
    <i class="fas fa-user-minus" inert></i>{{localize 'CAIRN.ApplyAttributeDamage' key=attribute}}
</button>
<button type="button" class="cairn-card-action apply-dmg apply-dmg-no-armor">
    <i class="fas fa-user-minus" inert></i>{{localize 'CAIRN.ApplyAttributeDamageNoArmor' key=attribute}}
</button>
{{else}}
<button type="button" class="cairn-card-action apply-dmg">
    <i class="fas fa-user-minus" inert></i>{{localize 'CAIRN.ApplyDamage'}}
</button>
{{/if}}
{{/if}}
